    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Augustus created the province from western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a>, with its capital at the veteran colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerita-augusta">Emerita Augusta</a>.</li><li>Farming, mining and fish-salting made it prosperous, and its monuments at Mérida and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcantara-bridge">Alcántara</a> still stand.</li><li>The Alans and then the Suebi ended Roman rule by 439, but its name survives as a classical name for Portugal.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Roman writers repeated a legend that Lusitanian mares could conceive from the west wind, which was said to explain the remarkable speed of their foals.</p></aside>
    </section>

